        {
            "_id": "GbCblles7vNIYNIC",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/OneAction.webp",
            "name": "Speak to Inner Evils",
            "sort": 400000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 1
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The Heart of Sarnax speaks to a creature it can hear the heartbeat of within 60 feet, beckoning that creature to give in to their inner desires to commit evil acts. The Heart of Sarnax attempts an Intimidation check against the target's Will DC, with the following results.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The inner evils take over fully, and the target becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Confused] for 1 minute. While confused, the creature will never attack the Heart of Sarnax, attacking themself instead if the Heart of Sarnax is the only viable target. The Heart of Sarnax becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Quickened] for 1 round, and can use the extra action only to Speak to Inner Evils.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The inner evils take over only briefly. The creature becomes confused for 1 round.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The inner evils fail to take over fully but are still distracting. The creature becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] until the end of their next turn.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature resists their inner evils and is immune to Speak to Inner Evils from this point on. The Heart of Sarnax recoils in shock, taking @Damage[4d6[mental]] damage (@Check[will|dc:25|basic] save).</p>"
                },
                "frequency": {
                    "max": 1,
                    "per": "round"
                },
